s implies that multiplying a function $f(t)$ by ${e}^{at}$ shifts the corresponding Laplace transform horizontally along the $s$-axis.\n\n- If $a>0,$ the graph of $F(s)$ shifts to the right.\n\n- If $a<0,$ the graph of $F(s)$ shifts to the left.\n\nIn our case, to get the graph of $L{{e}^{8t}f(t)},$ we must shift the graph of $F(s)$ by $8$ units to the right." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072996/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a516a99ebdb67ce5af57eb2ee27b6e39e7c23f318e5ad08f9e363fa48dbe171"} {"question" "q-332063" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072996/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5a00194a376d3e0a6746015e9008f5e5e35581856d7f79571d604fe69cef85a7"} {"question" "q-332063" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072996/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a516a99ebdb67ce5af57eb2ee27b6e39e7c23f318e5ad08f9e363fa48dbe171"} {"question" "q-332063" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "Scale the graph of $F(s)$ by a scale factor of $8$ horizontally."] ["text" "Scale the graph of $F(s)$ by a scale factor of $8$ vertically."] ["text" "Shift the graph of $F(s)$ by $8$ units to the left."] ["text" "Shift the graph of $F(s)$ by $8$ units to the right."] ["text" "The Laplace transform is unchanged."]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072996/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a516a99ebdb67ce5af57eb2ee27b6e39e7c23f318e5ad08f9e363fa48dbe171"} {"question" "q-332063" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "Shift the graph of $F(s)$ by $8$ units to the right."] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072996/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a516a99ebdb67ce5af57eb2ee27b6e39e7c23f318e5ad08f9e363fa48dbe171"} {"question" "q-331791" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider a function $y(t)$ such that its Laplace transform is $L{y(t)}=Y(s)$ for $s>{s}_{0}.$ Suppose we wish to find $L{{e}^{4t}y(t)}.$ Select the correct options in the reasoning below.By definition of the Laplace transform, we can write \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{e}^{4t}y(t)} & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{{field-1}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{{field-2}}\\,y(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={{field-3}}\\,\\text{for}\\,{{field-4}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072996/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a516a99ebdb67ce5af57eb2ee27b6e39e7c23f318e5ad08f9e363fa48dbe171"} {"question" "q-331791" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Starting from the definition of the Laplace transform, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{e}^{4t}y(t)} & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}\\cdot {e}^{4t}\\,y(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-(s-4)t}\\,y(t)\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall that $Y(s)={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}\\,y(t)\\,\\text{d}t,$ where $s>{s}_{0}.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-(s-4)t}\\,y(t)\\,\\text{d}t=Y(s-4),\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\ns-4>{s}_{0}\\,⇒\\,s>{s}_{0}+4.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072996/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a516a99ebdb67ce5af57eb2ee27b6e39e7c23f318e5ad08f9e363fa48dbe171"} {"question" "q-331791" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072996/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5a00194a376d3e0a6746015e9008f5e5e35581856d7f79571d604fe69cef85a7"} {"question" "q-331791" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072996/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a516a99ebdb67ce5af57eb2ee27b6e39e7c23f318e5ad08f9e363fa48dbe171"} {"question" "q-331791" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{e}^{-st}\\cdot {e}^{-4t}y(t)"] ["math" "{e}^{-st}\\cdot {e}^{4t}y(t)"] ["math" "{e}^{st}\\cdot {e}^{-4t}y(t)"] ["math" "{e}^{st}\\cdot {e}^{4t}y(t)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072996/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a516a99ebdb67ce5af57eb2ee27b6e39e7c23f318e5ad08f9e363fa48dbe171"} {"question" "q-331791" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{e}^{-st}\\cdot {e}^{4t}y(t)"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072996/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a516a99ebdb67ce5af57eb2ee27b6e39e7c23f318e5ad08f9e363fa48dbe171"} {"question" "q-331791" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072996/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a516a99ebdb67ce5af57eb2ee27b6e39e7c23f318e5ad08f9e363fa48dbe171"} {"question" "q-331791" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{e}^{(s+4)t}"] ["math" "{e}^{(s-4)t}"] ["math" "{e}^{-(s+4)t}"] ["math" "{e}^{-(s-4)t}"]] "category" "ma_comple