Starting from the definition of the Laplace transform, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{e}^{2t}f(t)} & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}\\cdot {e}^{2t}\\,f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-(s-2)t}\\,f(t)\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall that $F(s)={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}\\,f(t)\\,\\text{d}t,$ where $s>{s}_{0}.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-(s-2)t}\\,f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=F(s-2),\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\ns-2>{s}_{0}\\,⇒\\,s>{s}_{0}+2.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072996/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a516a99ebdb67ce5af57eb2ee27b6e39e7c23f318e5ad08f9e363fa48dbe171"} {"question" "q-328705" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072996/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5a00194a376d3e0a6746015e9008f5e5e35581856d7f79571d604fe69cef85a7"} {"question" "q-328705" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072996/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a516a99ebdb67ce5af57eb2ee27b6e39e7c23f318e5ad08f9e363fa48dbe171"} {"question" "q-328705" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{e}^{-st}\\cdot {e}^{-2t}f(t)"] ["math" "{e}^{-st}\\cdot {e}^{2t}f(t)"] ["math" "{e}^{-st}\\cdot {e}^{2}f(t)"] ["math" "{e}^{st}\\cdot {e}^{2t}f(t)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072996/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a516a99ebdb67ce5af57eb2ee27b6e39e7c23f318e5ad08f9e363fa48dbe171"} {"question" "q-328705" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math 